{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Do not harass Moab.</b> Regarding these nations — Seir, Ammon, and Moab — the Holy One, blessed be He, needed to warn Israel, for they thought to conquer them legitimately: Seir, because in many places Scripture calls them Chivim, and the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the Chivim to Israel as an inheritance. Therefore it is written: ״ובשעיר ישבו החורים לפנים״ — their original name was not Chivi, and they are not among the seven nations. And the reason Scripture calls them Chivi is as the Sages, may their memory be blessed, said: that they would sniff the land like a חויא (snake). Further on he explains where the Chivi that the Holy One, blessed be He, gave to Israel is. And likewise with Ammon and Moab, they thought that they were the land of the Refa'im that the Holy One, blessed be He, gave to Abraham, as it is written: ״את הקיני ואת הקנזי״ etc. ״ואת החוי ואת הפרזי ואת הרפאים״, and likewise it is written regarding Moab: ״רפאים יחשבו״ — also they, people thought and reckoned that it is the land of the Refa'im, but it is not so, for the Moabites call them Emim, because their terror is cast upon all creatures, and they have no claim in their land. And regarding Ammon it is written: ״ארץ רפאים תחשב גם היא״ — that is, people also thought that it was the land of the Refa'im, but it is not so, for the Ammonites call them Zamzumim, because they were masters of thought and intrigue. And all these were a numerous and great and tall people, like the Anakim. And because they trusted in their wisdom and their might, they rebelled against the Holy One, blessed be He, and He destroyed them and delivered them into the hands of those weaker than they. But the other nations, against whose land Israel had no claim whatever, needed no warning."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:27.523318463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}